[/TABLE]

Again, several points worth noting:

[LIST=1]
[*]The exact solve's 100% is definitional — it hits the target, so both metrics go to zero.
[*]Look instead at the exact solve's raw column: those countries were already 19% to 20% off on mean deviation, with the worst stratum 39% to 56% off. Countries where the exact solve is feasible are not "already roughly correct"; they are just as far off, they simply happen to land inside the cone.
[*]The approximation is the real body of cases, 236 to 407 countries. L1 improves 43% to 67%, bringing mean deviation from around 30% down to roughly 10%; Linf improves about 50%, bringing the worst stratum from 69% off down to 35%.
[/LIST]

[B]4.3 Prefilter effect[/B]

The size filter blocks a lot of countries. What does it cost and what does it buy?

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Item[/TH][TH]1337.10[/TH][TH]1386.03[/TH][TH]1743.04[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]countries filtered[/TD][TD]965 (67.0%)[/TD][TD]629 (59.4%)[/TD][TD]261 (44.3%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]location traversal given up[/TD][TD]1,751 (13.1%)[/TD][TD]1,176 (8.7%)[/TD][TD]521 (2.7%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]of which exactly solvable[/TD][TD]0 (0.0%)[/TD][TD]2 (0.3%)[/TD][TD]0 (0.0%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]of which approximable[/TD][TD]565 (58.5%)[/TD][TD]390 (62.0%)[/TD][TD]113 (43.3%)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]of which unsolvable anyway[/TD][TD]400 (41.5%)[/TD][TD]237 (37.7%)[/TD][TD]148 (56.7%)[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

The benefit is clear: it blocks 40% to 70% of countries while giving up only 2.7% to 13.1% of location traversal, with little impact on population demand balance.

The cost needs separating out. [B]Almost no exact solves are sacrificed[/B], which matches expectation: below four locations the matrix has at most 3 non-empty columns and cannot cover four strata. What is actually given up is approximation opportunity — 43% to 62% of the filtered countries could have received an approximate solution.

This is a performance decision. Adding the prefilter costs little while cutting sweep triggers substantially. In measurement, only with the prefilter in place does monthly computation reach an imperceptible level.

